The shared parser interprets day-first dates month first. R-41200 records 7 April becoming 4 July. Booking v3 has a separate problem: its hint says MM/DD/YYYY even when the form reads the tenant’s day-first order. R-41230 records 6 January becoming 1 June.

Count each report ID once, then use the tenant locale, form version and report channel to assign its cause. The browser-based intake tags disagree with that classification in both directions.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Review the one-day moves separately before closing the parser ticket. A one-day shift is a different symptom from a month/day swap.

